'a stable, high-ROCE model.'\n- Client base spans government/defence (Rashtrapati Bhawan rooftop project, CRPF, BSF, CISF) and industrial/commercial names (Golf Ceramics, Pragna Pharma, Pragna Dyechem, Uma Kraft Paper, Reliance Jio, Futaba Industrial), reflecting a diversified customer mix across captive and non-captive projects.","src":"deck","as_of":"29-06-2026"},"capital_allocation":{"title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)","body":"- States a deliberate 'balanced approach' where EPC generates immediate cash flows and RESCO builds long-term annuity value, explicitly described as creating 'a stable, high-ROCE model.'\n- Converted to a Public Limited company in 2024 (authorised capital ₹25 Cr) and listed on BSE in 2026, providing a public-market capital base to fund RESCO asset build-out via subsidiaries GRE Green Energy Private Limited and GRE Green Assets.","src":"deck","as_of":"29-06-2026"},"other":{"title":"Notable from the deck","body":"- [Corporate History] Originally incorporated in 1999 as GRE Electronics Pvt Ltd (CFL products); entered LED manufacturing and established wholly-owned US subsidiary D K USA Inc. in 2015; strategically pivoted to solar as its core focus in 2013-14; renamed GRE Renew Enertech in 2023 ahead of its 2024 conversion to Public Limited and 2026 BSE listing.","src":"deck","as_of":"29-06-2026"}}}